
EXERCISE 7: Network Scanning with Nmap
Date: 14. Aug. 2026
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Aim: To study and perform network scanning using Nmap to discover hosts, open ports, and
services.
Tools Required: Kali Linux, Metasploitable2, Nmap.
Theory:
Nmap (Network Mapper) is a free, open-source tool for network discovery and security
auditing. It is used to:
 Discover live hosts on a network
 Identify open ports
 Detect operating systems and service versions
 Perform vulnerability scanning using NSE scripts
Common Scan Types:
 TCP SYN Scan (-sS): Stealthy, default for root.
 TCP Connect Scan (-sT): Full connection, used without root.
 UDP Scan (-sU): Scans UDP ports.
 Version Detection (-sV): Identifies service versions.
 OS Detection (-O): Identifies operating system.
Procedure:
1. Find the target IP:
ifconfig
Assume target is 192.168.56.101.
2. Basic scan:
nmap 192.168.56.101
3. Scan specific ports:
nmap -p 21,22,23,80 192.168.56.101
4. Scan all ports:
nmap -p- 192.168.56.101
5. Service version detection:
nmap -sV 192.168.56.101
USC24301J, Basics of Ethical Hacking for Cyber Security
15
6. OS detection:
sudo nmap -O 192.168.56.101
7. Aggressive scan:
sudo nmap -A 192.168.56.101
8. Save output:
nmap -sV -oN nmap_scan.txt 192.168.56.101
